/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-04-13T08:42:18-07:00","id":864967,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/864756-references-to-less-known-hosts?p=864919#post864919\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That reminds me, I still need to write up the lampreys' progenitor and, possibly, the notional slowly-turning-into-Kindred-vampires lampreys akin to what's happening with the Jiang Shi.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh yeah, that would be nice indeed and leech hosts initially inspired me with much the same idea. That said the peculiar way they interact with the Gauntlet and manipulate it as water bodies made me think a little of <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Beaver_dam\" target=\"_blank\">beaver dams</a> and if i could somehow work something - or preferably some other predatory/parasitic animal with a somewhat similar habit - out of it to really mess with and catch my players off-guard.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1147-baaldam","name":"Baaldam","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1147_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4937"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}